# Alacrium Portable for Windows README.txt

## Copyright (c) 2026 Alex313031

# How to use the files in this .zip
# Unpack .zip to wherever

Contains ALACRIUM.BAT for running portable/standalone.
	- Also contains ALACRIUM_SHELL.BAT for running the Alacrium Content Shell.

Append --disable-encryption --disable-machine-id to ALACRIUM.BAT to disable user profile encryption and tying it to a specific machine, to enable truly portable usage.
 Note that this will remove things like passwords and history the first time it is enabled, so back up your stuff or make a new user profile.

You can also skip using ALACRIUM.BAT and just copy the contents of BIN somewhere, and run alacrium.exe from within.
 Note this will make a profile dir in C:\Users\$USERNAME\AppData\Local\Alacrium\User Data\ and write a few registry values.

BIN - Contains Alacrium
	- Contains alacrium_shell.ico for setting an icon for alacrium_shell.exe if you make a shortcut.

USER_DATA - Contains user profile data.

Thanks for using Alacrium and feel free to use the issues or discussions for problems, questions, features, or suggestions.

	- Alex313031
